  "body": "This commit delivers three artifacts related to the Hierarchical Reasoning Model (HRM):\r\n\r\n1.  `HRM_inference_colab.py`: A Python script with commented-out cells designed to be easily used in a Google Colab notebook. It demonstrates how to download the HRM model, generate the ARC dataset, and run inference on a sample, including visualization of the results.\r\n\r\n2.  `run_hrm_local.py`: A standalone, command-line Python script for running HRM inference on a local, CPU-only machine. It is designed for flexibility, taking repository, checkpoint, and data paths as arguments.\r\n\r\n3.  `HRM_for_X-Ray_Analysis.md`: A detailed research report outlining a strategy for adapting the HRM model for chest x-ray analysis. It covers the necessary model configuration changes, analyzes the minimal impact on model size, and proposes a training strategy using sequential patching.",
